<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inter caetera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1493</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inter caetera is a papal bull issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-vi">Pope Alexander VI</a> in 1493, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s first voyage. It granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> rights over lands discovered to the west of a line in the Atlantic, dividing spheres of exploration with Portugal. It provided a legal and religious basis for the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inter-caetera.jpg" alt="Inter caetera" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tzzzpfff at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%BCdamerika1650.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
